Package: ecoconnectivity
Title: Multi-Resolution Landscape Connectivity
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Roozbeh", "Valavi", email = "roozbeh.valavi@csiro.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organisation",
           role = "cph"))
Description: Calculates landscape connectedness and the Bioclimatic Ecosystem
    Resilience Index on in-memory raster arrays using the 'connectivity-core'
    Rust numerical engine. Provides a native R interface without a Python
    runtime dependency. This initial development interface operates on matrices
    and arrays; raster file handling and tile planning are left to the caller.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/csiro/connectivity
BugReports: https://github.com/csiro/connectivity/issues
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
NeedsCompilation: yes
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 8.0.0
Config/rextendr/version: 0.5.0
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.86.0, GNU make, xz
Depends: 
    R (>= 4.2)
